msgid ""
"A sensor tool (GPU-Z / HWiNFO) \"Video Engine Load\", which reads the "
"driver directly rather than the OS per-process accounting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:59 aeb97960e2314ce3a3793e6d96e7eccb
msgid "The deletion safety gate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:61 1606a4e16250499bb0cbe443e3393897
msgid ""
"``verify`` is what makes deleting originals safe. For each source it "
"checks three things and only passes a file when all three hold:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:64 aa72d25f7ebf43b5b49ef6a19caf864e
msgid "**Completeness** — a converted file exists at the mirrored path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:65 3694075500814ef9b4cbf6f3f07cd42a
msgid ""
"**Length match** — converted duration equals the original within "
"tolerance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:66 67b4319149554cba9680b76f383d98f2
msgid "**Integrity** — a *full decode* of the converted file reports zero errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:68 20ba545d6bd04b7f9c339cb6769992ee
msgid ""
"Files that pass are marked ``SAFE-TO-DELETE``; anything else is ``KEEP-"
"SOURCE`` with the reason (missing, length mismatch, or decode errors). "
"The command writes the verdicts to ``_slimv_verify_report.csv`` and "
"**never deletes anything itself** — the decision stays yours. Delete only"
" the originals whose row says ``SAFE-TO-DELETE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:75 0d6d1ed7524c4dbe9970b572337f8be0
msgid "Watching a long run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/04-workflow.rst:77 67b3b72d5d6a4e38b389c699cf7dd18a
#, python-format
msgid ""
"``encode`` is resumable: if it is interrupted, re-running the same "
"command skips the files already done and continues. Keep an eye on free "
"disk space on the output drive — H.265 output is typically 40–55% of an "
"H.264 source, but a high-motion title can run larger. Deleting verified "
"sources as modules complete keeps space comfortable on a tight drive."
msgstr ""

